      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "About... well, three days.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:23",
      "end_timestamp": "00:26",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Right, right. Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:26",
      "end_timestamp": "00:37",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I get some relief from oral rehydration. I'd call it severe. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. I've had crampy tummy pain too, um, for one week. About crampy tummy pain, it's severe, honestly.",
      "start_timestamp": "00:38",
      "end_timestamp": "01:00",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]",
        "symptoms[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Alright, have you got any known allergies?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:01",
      "end_timestamp": "01:04",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I had a reaction to trimethoprim when I was younger, a rash, and I've avoided it since.",
